  "query_preview": "..\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nA broad trough remains over the northern Plains keeping\ntemperatures generally cool for mid-June. Ridge developing along\nthe west coast occasionally with try to push warmer air across the\ndivide, but the persistent and strong Hudson Bay low will maintain\nthe cooler northwest flow. \n\nA shortwave will push through the region on Friday, bringing a\nchance for showers or thunderstorms, and mixing winds. Lake Wind\nconditions are marginal but considering the under forecasting of\nmodel winds, will go ahead with Advisory for this afternoon. \n\nColder air slides into the region following the shortwave today,\nlingering through the weekend. Saturday night should be the\ncoldest night, before western ridge begins to push warmer air\nacross the divide. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nConfidence then remains above average for cool and unsettled \nweather for next several days given the NW flow continuing. \nConfidence in exact timing, placement, and amount of precipitation\nremains low to moderate given the mesoscale detail still to be \nworked out a larger time scales.\n\nMade slights adjustments to the pops and winds for today to\naccount for slight under forecasting of both recently.",
